      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Pulse Slate · MiniMax H3 — starter graph (Spectrum + Sage)\n\n## Where you type\nThe Director node carries **two boxes on its face**:\n\n- **GLOBAL PROMPT** — art style, lighting, camera rules, identity locks, score.\n  Optional line labels: `style:` `identity:` `retention:` `soundscape:` `music:`\n  Unlabelled text is treated as style.\n- **SHOT PROMPT** — one shot per line, each starting `[Shot N]` or `[MM:SS.mmm]`.\n  Shots without a timecode spread evenly between the ones that have them.\n\n## Never type a tag number\nReference bin assets by **name**: `@Image1`, `@Mimi`, `@[Cafe wide]`.\n`<Picture 3>` is assigned from bin order at compile time and shifts whenever the\nbin changes — a hand-typed number will describe the wrong asset and still render\nsuccessfully. The node reports any it finds.\n\n## Assets\nDrag images / video / audio **onto the node body**. No loader nodes needed.\nEach gets an alias (`Image1`, `Video1`, `Audio1`) you can rename inline.\nThe meter refuses a drop that would break the budget: 9 images, 3 videos,\n3 audio, **12 files total**.\n\n## Two output paths — pick by duration\n\n| duration | use | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **≤ 15s** (one window) | group **A** | node hands back `positive` + `latent`; your sampler runs |\n| **> 15s** (many windows) | group **B** | node renders internally per window and stitches |\n\nGroup A is enabled. For a long timeline, **mute A / unmute B**\n(select the group, press Ctrl+M).\n\n## Duration rules\n- Frames snap to **17k+5**; 362 (~15.08s) is the trained ceiling.\n- Every window is **≥124 frames** — a short tail merges backwards automatically.\n- Only a total under 124 frames renders as one short window.\n\n## cfg\nLeave at **1.0**. H3's own pipeline uses BasicGuider and has no negative\nconditioning anywhere. Above 1.0 switches to CFGGuider with an empty negative.\n\n## Model patches — and why they are upstream\n\nThis variant is the starter graph with the documented chain wired in:\n\n`UNETLoader → Spectrum (history_storage: system_ram) → Sage Attention → PulseSlate`\n\n**It has to be upstream.** Path B samples internally with the model handed\n*to* the node, so a patch applied to the node's `model` **output** would speed\nup the ≤15s path and do nothing at all for a long timeline — the case where it\nmatters most. The node warns when it is handed an unpatched model.\n\n**Spectrum's `system_ram` is not a speed setting.** It is what makes a\n362-frame window fit on a 32GB card. Switch it to `vram` and a full-length\nwindow is likely to fail with an out-of-memory error rather than run slowly.\n\n**These two node packs are not part of Pulse Studio and are not required.**\nInstall `ComfyUI-Spectrum-MiniMax-H3` and `ComfyUI-KJNodes`, or delete the\npatch column and wire the loaders straight into the director.\n\n## fl2va\nOnly connect `model_fl2va` if you set a first/last-frame branch. Both\ncheckpoints loaded at once is ~42GB.\n"
      ],
      "title": "READ ME"
    },
